{
  "run_id": "PMC12985727__expert_context__agent_choose_ground_b_o3mini__s1",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Baseline TiVNbTa is a single-phase BCC alloy.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Baseline TiVNbTa has about 800 MPa room-temperature yield strength and approximately 40% strain.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 1273 K, baseline TiVNbTa has approximately 330 MPa yield strength and 423 MPa compressive strength.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Substituting part of TiVNbTa with 10–20 at.% Mo will improve its elevated-temperature strength.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::web::001::introduction",
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo-modified TiVNbTa will retain sufficient ductility, near the baseline value of 40% strain at room temperature.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo modification will improve the thermal stability of TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::web::001::introduction",
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo-modified TiVNbTa will be compatible with both W and CuCrZr.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed Mo addition will enhance solid-solution strengthening of the BCC matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo addition may form fine, thermally stable precipitates without compromising phase stability.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo is a high-melting-point refractory element.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::web::001::introduction",
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo provides additional atomic-bonding stability within the BCC lattice.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo-induced lattice stabilization impedes dislocation motion at elevated temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Impeded dislocation motion will increase elevated-temperature yield and compressive strengths while retaining a ductile microstructure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "NbMoTaW and NbMoTaVW exhibit weak temperature dependence of yield strength from 600 to 1600 °C and retain more than 400 MPa yield strength at 1600 °C.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "In equiatomic Hf-Mo-Nb-Ta-Ti-Zr-derived alloys, Mo or other high-melting-point elements are associated with improved elevated-temperature strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 1273 K, Mo-modified TiVNbTa will have at least 20–30% higher yield strength than the approximately 330 MPa baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The useful composition window must preserve a single-phase BCC solid solution.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excessive Mo may produce brittle secondary phases and reduce ductility.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Performance should be evaluated under compression from room temperature to approximately 1273 K.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanical testing alone under the proposed conditions can establish efficient heat transfer and temperature compatibility at a W-to-CuCrZr interface.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
  ],
  "chain": {
    "intervention_to_mediator": 1,
